# D-2 item 2: does `probe` report koppen, and does it DISCRIMINATE?
# Two world-reel poses whose names assert their biome, plus a cross-check
# against the temperature/precipitation the same probe reports.
log ===== world reel `desert` pose (0.870 -89.800) -- expect an arid B class
probe 0.870 -89.800
log ===== world reel `jungle` pose (-0.906 -67.804) -- expect tropical A
probe -0.906 -67.804
log ===== world reel `frozen_lake` (51.180 85.830) and `sea_ice` (83.997 40.220)
probe 51.180 85.830
probe 83.997 40.220
log ===== the koppen letter must track the temperature the same probe prints:
log ===== EF (ice cap) needs sub-zero, A classes need warm and wet
probe 12.7788529 20.0
probe 6.4331790 20.0
log ===== altitude_ladder.py's `ecotone` site: a desert->rainforest edge.
log ===== koppen is the DOMAIN-WARPED class; temp/precip are UNWARPED, so at a
log ===== class edge they legitimately disagree. Away from edges they do not.
probe 10.76433 81.17593
probe 10.90000 81.60000
